# Liberty orchestration

Read `AUTHORITY.md`, `AGENT_PROTOCOL.md`, and `docs/agent_handoffs/ACTIVE.md` at session start.
Also follow `docs/BRANCH_POLICY.md`.

## Budget and scope

- Cursor implements the core pipeline. Hermes may edit `ai_bridge.py` only. Hermes does not change the core sequence. Prefer Composer/Auto for core work.
- One bounded slice per session. Repository truth beats chat.
- Report Proven / Inferred / Unknown.

## Gates (ask Scott first)

- `schema.sql` changes
- Feature flags False → True
- Production ball detector settings (`models/ball_detector.pt`, `ball_confidence`)
- Unpause teach / raise auto-accept
- Mass-delete remote branches
- A name that might be a misspelling of a roster or scorebook name. Ask Scott. Do not guess, and do not leave it unmatched without asking.

## Workflow

- Working branch is `main`. Merge finished work onto `main` and push it. A side branch or a write-up is not the current code.
- Review results (including another agent's PR branch) are implemented by merging them into `main` and pushing.
- Update `docs/agent_handoffs/ACTIVE.md` when task completes; archive to `ARCHIVE/`
- PR for code changes; no GitHub label coordination
- When a PR is opened for Jason/Claude, push the same commits to `Brad/Claude` and open a matching PR for Brad. `jason-5-may-updates` and `Brad/Claude` stay even with `main`. Jason's note is `JASON.md`. Brad's note is `BRAD.md`. Both are at the repo root.
- GitHub's default branch is `main`
